## Priority 1 \'97 Inline post-submit confirmation message\
\
**Problem:**\
After form submission the user is redirected to `thankyou.html` via a\
hidden iframe `onload` trigger. The original brief specified an inline\
confirmation message on the same page without navigation.\
\
**Why it matters:**\
On mobile a full-page redirect can feel like an error. An inline message\
is faster, clearer and better UX. It also keeps the user on the page\
where they can still share or explore.\
\
**Suggested solution:**\
1. Remove the hidden iframe and `onload` redirect\
2. Use the Fetch API to POST the form data to Google Forms asynchronously\
3. On success, hide the form and show a hidden `<div>` with the message:\
   *"You're on the list. We'll contact you when we launch in your area."*\
4. Keep `thankyou.html` for direct URL visits and social sharing\
\
```javascript\
// Outline approach\
form.addEventListener('submit', async function(e) \{\
  e.preventDefault();\
  const data = new FormData(form);\
  await fetch(form.action, \{ method: 'POST', body: data, mode: 'no-cors' \});\
  form.style.display = 'none';\
  document.getElementById('form-success').style.display = 'block';\
\});\
```\
\
**Effort:** Low \'97 approximately 20 lines replacing existing form script.\
\
